Both are "fixture strictness vs emergent/statistical behavior" issues:
- The walk-based chain finder (`findPlayableChain`) sometimes can't reach a 3-run even when one exists (dead-end walks). This is a *fixture* limitation, and it also slightly affects the assertion "applied ≥ 190". The honest fix: measure the fixture's own effectiveness, i.e. assert that the board invariants hold (full, playable, no deadlock) and that "applied" is a reasonable fraction; ALSO improve the chain finder to be exhaustive rather than random-walk (a small BFS/DFS that finds *any* chain of length ≥3 — that's deterministic and stronger).

Better: replace the naive random walk with a **deterministic exhaustive search** for a chain of length ≥ MinChainLength: a bounded DFS from every start cell, returning a path of the required length. With ≤49 cells and a depth-3/4 search, cost is trivial, and it will find a chain whenever one exists → `applied` becomes ~200/200 and the chain quality improves.

That's a fixture improvement, not a game change. Let me rewrite `walkChainFrom`/`findPlayableChain` into a deterministic `findChain(board, minLength, maxLength)` using DFS with backtracking:

```ts
/** 在棋盘上确定性地找一条长度 ≥ minLength 的同色相邻路径（找不到返回空）。 */
export function findChain(board: Board, minLength: number, maxLength: number): number[] {
	const total = board.columns * board.rows;
	for (let start = 0; start < total; start++) {
		const col = start % board.columns;
		const row = Math.floor(start / board.columns);
		const type = board.cellIndex(col, row);
		if (type < 0) continue;
		const used: boolean[] = [];
		for (let i = 0; i < total; i++) used.push(false);
		const path: number[] = [start];
		used[start] = true;
		if (growPath(board, path, used, type, minLength, maxLength)) return path;
	}
	return [];
}

/** 深度优先扩展路径，直到长度达到 minLength（最多到 maxLength）。 */
function growPath(board: Board, path: number[], used: boolean[], type: number, minLength: number, maxLength: number): boolean {
	if (path.length >= minLength) return true;
	if (path.length >= maxLength) return false;
	const last = path[path.length - 1];
	const col = last % board.columns;
	const row = Math.floor(last / board.columns);
	const options: number[] = [];
	collectOption(board, options, used, col - 1, row, type);
	collectOption(board, options, used, col + 1, row, type);
	collectOption(board, options, used, col, row - 1, type);
	collectOption(board, options, used, col, row + 1, type);
	for (const next of options) {
		used[next] = true;
		path.push(next);
		if (growPath(board, path, used, type, minLength, maxLength)) return true;
		path.pop();
		used[next] = false;
	}
	return false;
}
