But careful: setPosition sets baseX/baseY permanently. After animation ends, resetFallPositions sets them to correct centers. Good.

Hook in update(dt): add `this.advanceFall(dt);` at start.

Also `endFlash()` calls refreshFromBoard() — that doesn't touch positions, fine.

One concern: `refreshFromBoard` is called by Game right after animateFall. During the flash, cleared cells hidden. The fallen block lands into a cleared cell (hidden). After flash ends → endFlash → refreshFromBoard shows it. Position already reset. Good.

