Confirmed: `'str' + number` transpiles to `.. tostring(...)`. So `'' + turns` becomes `'' .. tostring(turns)` → safe.

Now implement.

1. `game/ui/BlockWidget.ts`:
- add fields: `private badge: Label.Type | undefined = undefined; private lockTurns = 0;`
- `setLocked(on)`: when turning off, also clear badge text (set lockTurns = 0 and hide badge). Keep early return but handle badge clearing.
- `setLockTurns(turns)`: clamp `turns < 0 → 0`; if equal to current → return; store; ensure badge; set `badge.text = '' + turns`, `badge.visible = turns > 0 && this.locked`; redraw.
   Ordering issue: refreshFromBoard calls setLocked then setLockTurns. If setLockTurns called with same value as before but locked changed... e.g. cell stays locked across refresh with same turns → no-op, fine. After unlock: setLocked(false) → clears badge; then setLockTurns(0) → already 0 → no-op. Fine.
   But what if setLocked(false) early-returns because already false while lockTurns > 0? Can't happen since transitions are consistent.

   Hmm, but caution: `setLocked` early return when `this.locked === on`. Add badge clearing inside — but only when actually transitioning. Let me restructure:

```ts
setLocked(on: boolean): void {
	if (this.locked === on) {
		return;
	}
	this.locked = on;
	if (!on) {
		// 解锁后不再显示剩余次数
		this.lockTurns = 0;
		this.applyBadge();
	}
	this.redraw();
}
```
where `applyBadge()` sets badge text/visible. But careful: `applyBadge` requires badge created. Let me create badge lazily only when turns > 0 to avoid 49 extra labels (fine either way; 49 labels is nothing, but lazily is nicer). Actually simpler & more robust: create the badge in the constructor for every block widget (49 labels, tiny). That avoids lazy-undefined branches. Cost: 49 labels — acceptable? The block widgets already each have a DrawNode + Label. 49 more labels is fine.

But wait: `Label(...)` returns undefined possibly — handle with the undefined check.

I'll create it in the constructor, positioned top-right, small, and hidden by default.

Layout: cell size = size. Badge at `Vec2(size - size*0.22, size - size*0.2)` with anchor... Label inherits anchor property; default anchor (0.5, 0.5)? Label anchor default is (0,0)? For Labels in Dora, the `Label` node's anchor defaults... The existing glyph uses `label.position = Vec2(size/2, size/2)` and label.text centered — that implies default anchor centers the text (standard Dora Label anchor default (0.5,0.5)). Yes, Dora Label default anchor is (0.5,0.5) (Node default is Vec2(0.5,0.5)).

So place badge center at `Vec2(size - size * 0.26, size - size * 0.26)`.

Add a dark disc behind it: in drawSelf when locked && lockTurns > 0, `this.canvas.drawDot(Vec2(size - r - pad, size - r - pad), r, Color(20, 22, 28, 235))` where r = size*0.22. Draw after the polygon so it's on top. Does `DrawNode.drawDot` exist in this project's usage? Plan says drawDot available. Confirm DrawNode has drawDot: yes (baseline mentions drawDot).

Also, once unlocked the disc disappears (redraw called by setLocked) — but note when `setLockTurns(0)` called on an unlocked widget it does no-op, and drawSelf is already correct because locked=false.

Careful ordering in drawSelf: polygon fill then dot then maybe a thin ring. Fine.

Badge text color: bright amber `Color(255, 214, 120, 255)`, font `Math.max(12, Math.floor(size * 0.3))`.

